To correct the app lifecycle pattern conceptually, you must move the registration of MOOS variables from OnStartUp() to OnConnectToServer().
The Conceptual Error
The issue occurs because OnStartUp() is only called once when the MOOS application process first launches
1
. In contrast, a reconnection to the MOOSDB starts a fresh communication session. Since the MOOSDB does not maintain a permanent memory of an app's previous interests, a newly connected (or reconnected) app is responsible for informing the database of what mail it needs
2
.
If your Register() calls are trapped in OnStartUp(), they will not be re-executed when the app reconnects, leaving the app with zero active subscriptions in the new session
2
3
.
Corrected Lifecycle Pattern
The standard practice is to perform registrations in OnConnectToServer(), which is triggered every time a connection is established with the server
3
4
.
bool MyApp::OnStartUp()
{
  // Use this for reading configuration parameters from the .moos file [1]
  return true;
}

bool MyApp::OnConnectToServer()
{
  // Use this for registering for MOOS variables [3]
  // This ensures subscriptions are renewed after a reconnect
  Register("NAV_X", 0); 
  return true;
}

Recommended Practice: The registerVariables() Helper
Many MOOS developers use a dedicated helper function to avoid duplicating code and to ensure registrations happen both at the initial launch and during any subsequent reconnections
3
.
void MyApp::registerVariables()
{
  // If using AppCasting, call the superclass method first [3]
  // AppCastingMOOSApp::RegisterVariables(); 

  Register("NAV_X", 0);
}

bool MyApp::OnStartUp()
{
  // ... process config ...
  return true;
}

bool MyApp::OnConnectToServer()
{
  registerVariables();
  return true;
}

Diagnostic Checklist for Reconnect Issues
Check Registration Location: Verify that Register() is called inside OnConnectToServer() rather than just OnStartUp()
3
.
Verify DB Connectivity: Use uXMS or uQueryDB to confirm the app is listed in DB_CLIENTS after the reconnect
5
more_horiz
.
Check Variable Scope: Scope the variable (e.g., NAV_X) after a reconnect to see if the MOOSDB is actually receiving new posts from the source
8
9
.
Inspect AppCasts: If the app is AppCast-enabled, check the "Subscriptions" section in pMarineViewer or uMAC to see if NAV_X is actively being tracked
